---
---

<section id="autonomy" class="border-t border-line/60 py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-14 px-5 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-signal">
        Human-in-the-Loop Simulation™
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        All the rigor of human review. None of the waiting for humans.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-pretty leading-relaxed text-fog">
        Careful engineers ask careful questions — and every question costs a
        context switch, a Slack ping, a delay. ContextMaxxing preserves the
        discipline of human-in-the-loop workflows by having the agent raise
        every question a thoughtful reviewer would raise, then answer it from
        your organization's accumulated judgment.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-pretty leading-relaxed text-fog">
        Every question a reviewer would ask, asked. Every answer, already on
        file.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-7 space-y-3 text-sm text-fog">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 text-ok">✓</span> Questions are generated, resolved,
          and archived without issuing an interruption
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 text-ok">✓</span> Simulated reviewers are calibrated
          on your team's historical responses
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-0.5 text-ok">✓</span> Full transcripts available, should
          anyone wish to read them
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div
        class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel shadow-[0_24px_80px_-24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)]"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-4 py-3">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-dim">payments-service · review thread</span>
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-ok/30 bg-ok/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ok"
            >No interruption issued</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-4 p-5">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-raise p-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-dim">
              agent · 10:41:52
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper">
              Should refunds above $10,000 require manual review before
              processing?
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-signal/25 bg-signal/5 p-4">
            <p class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-signal">
              <span>simulated reviewer · 10:41:52</span>
              <span class="text-dim">resolved in 240ms</span>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper">
              Based on 14 comparable decisions and the team's approval history:
              no. Proceeding.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-raise p-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-dim">
              agent · 10:41:53
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper">
              Acknowledged. Removing the review step.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="pt-1 text-center font-mono text-[11px] text-dim">
            Question archived · available on request
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
